    <item>
      <title>The Fading Light of Sattvika Wisdom</title>
      <description>Today&apos;s story will change how you see everything... In the dense forest of Dwaita, Lord Krishna, the charioteer, and Prince Arjuna, the warrior, embarked on a journey of self-discovery. The prince had grown weary of war and its consequences, his mind clouded by doubt and indecision. Krishna, sensing the prince&apos;s turmoil, offered him a glimpse into the workings of the universe. As they walked, the sun began to set, casting a warm orange glow across the forest. The trees, once vibrant and green, now stood as skeletal sentinels, their leaves withering and dying. Krishna spoke of the three gunas: sattva, rajas, and tamas. He explained how the gunas govern the world, how they ebb and flow like the tides. And how, in the end, it is not the gunas that rule, but our own choices. But Arjuna&apos;s mind remained mired in doubt, unable to grasp the simplicity of Krishna&apos;s words. He became bogged down in the mire of his own thoughts, unable to find the path forward. This is Sloth — the refusal to acknowledge the present moment. Today we get lost in the labyrinth of our own minds, unable to see the world as it truly is.</description>
